mod:redef_reroot_release_faces;
// 2026-11-18 (landing 177d2c, row 2 as F-c: rulings l.17976, l.18021, l.18074 and l.18105). Row 2 walks a pointer parameter's own slot THROUGH at a
// call's first targets, where main cut it, since the callee may write below it (redef_reroot_store_*.npk), and keeps every walk main makes. Its
// earlier forms were attacked. Its first form (P1) released 60 programs main refuses: R-1 (44), a store whose walk reached the pointer parameter
// above its last hop read as a store INTO its pointee; R-2 (16), a store below the pointee made in a nested call reached the caller as a FLOW with
// no MUT entry. Probing its next form (F-a, which told a write INTO a pointee from one below it) found 4 more of R-1, and the attacks on it and its
// probes found R-3, the releases of its INTO skip: a callee re-points the slot it is handed and writes below it, and F-a dropped the DEF-644 (B)
// reroot walk main makes there (rulings l.17940, l.18004, l.18105). R-3's class has 31 confirmed releases (x1 3, k 8, x2 20; 29 distinct programs,
// since `x2_s1d5a1_a1` is `x1_deep_a1`'s program and `x2_s1d1a1_a1` is `x1_deep4_a1`'s program), and every one is pinned here, so the re-planned
// INTO lift faces each. F-a is withdrawn (l.17976): no skip of a walk main makes can be shown safe while DEF-685's and DEF-348's lines are open,
// and the INTO lift is re-planned after they close. Each release is a freed read (236 at -O0 and -O2, 97 under the detector), refused on main
// (524cf77) and here. THE PINS (96): one per release (95), at main's sites (R-1 48, R-2 16, R-3 31), and one more of main's refusals that no form
// released, the depth of a write two pointers down (`r2f_dp1_wa_a1`). Their controls are in redef_reroot_release_ok.npk, but for `c14_sf_r1` and
// `c14_sf_r2`, which main refuses at BORROW-009.
error:E5;
